<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="u4b-ct-labeled">
  <title>Unit 4b Subgoal Labeled Puzzles for Toggle Code</title>
  <p>
    These are copies of the ArrayList Mixed Up Code Practice puzzles with
    subgoal labels added. The ArrayList Toggle Code Practice page uses them as
    the Get Help puzzles for its write code problems. Each loop header and its
    opening brace are one block, so one label sits on each loop, and each if or
    else is one block with its body.
  </p>

  <activity label="ch8ex1muc-sgl" xml:id="ch8ex1muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following program segment should be a class that creates an
        ArrayList called <c>conversation</c>, adds in some elements
        (<c>"hello"</c>, <c>"goodbye"</c>, <c>"how are you"</c>, and <c>"see you
        later"</c>), and prints out the elements with <c>", "</c> after each. But,
        the blocks have been mixed up and include extra blocks that are not
        needed in a correct solution. Drag the needed code from the left to the
        right and put them in order with the correct indention so that the code
        would work correctly. Click the Check button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="2">
        <cline>import java.util.ArrayList;</cline>
        <cline>import java.util.List;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <cline>public class ListTest</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <cline>    public static void main(String[] args)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>        // Create the list to hold the phrases</cline>
        <cline>        ArrayList&lt;String&gt; conversation;</cline>
        <cline>        conversation = new ArrayList&lt;String&gt;();</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Store the four phrases in the list</cline>
          <cline>        conversation.add("hello");</cline>
          <cline>        conversation.add("goodbye");</cline>
          <cline>        conversation.add("how are you");</cline>
          <cline>        conversation.add("see you later");</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Store the four phrases in the list</cline>
          <cline>        conversation[0] = "hello";</cline>
          <cline>        conversation[1] = "goodbye";</cline>
          <cline>        conversation[2] = "how are you";</cline>
          <cline>        conversation[3] = "see you later";</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Store the four phrases in the list</cline>
          <cline>        conversation.add("hello", "goodbye", "how are you", "see you later");</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <cline>        // Use an enhanced for-each loop to visit each element of the list</cline>
        <cline>        for (String element : conversation)</cline>
        <cline>        {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>            // Print the phrase without moving to a new line</cline>
        <cline>            System.out.print(element + ", ");</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="8">
        <cline>        } // end for loop</cline>
        <cline>    } // end main method</cline>
        <cline>} // end of class</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="ch8ex2muc-sgl" xml:id="ch8ex2muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following program segment should be a method that traverses through
        an ArrayList of Strings (the parameter) and print out the elements in
        reverse order – so {“cat”, “dog”, “mouse”} should print “mouse, dog,
        cat, ” as output. Assume the ArrayList “myList” has been instantiated
        and filled with Strings. But, the blocks have been mixed up and include
        extra blocks that are not needed in a correct solution. Drag the
        needed blocks from the left and put them in the correct order on the
        right. Click the Check button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="3">
        <cline>public static void printBackwards(ArrayList&lt;String&gt; myList)</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>    // Use a for loop to visit each index of the list back to front</cline>
          <cline>    for (int i = myList.size() - 1; i &gt;= 0; i--)</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>    // Use a for loop to visit each index of the list back to front</cline>
          <cline>    for (int i = myList.size() - 1; i &gt; 0; i--)</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>    // Use a for loop to visit each index of the list back to front</cline>
          <cline>    for (int i = myList.size(); i &gt;= 0; i--)</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Print the element at this index without moving to a new line</cline>
          <cline>        System.out.print(myList.get(i) + ", ");</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Print the element at this index without moving to a new line</cline>
          <cline>        System.out.print(myList[i] + ", ");</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>    } // end for loop</cline>
        <cline>} // end printBackwards method</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="ch8ex3muc-sgl" xml:id="ch8ex3muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following program segment should remove all the zeros from an
        ArrayList of Integers. Assume the ArrayList “listOfNums” has been
        instantiated and filled with Integers. But, the blocks have been mixed
        up and include extra blocks that are not needed in a correct
        solution. Drag the blocks from the left and put them in the correct
        order on the right. Click the Check button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="4">
        <cline>// Start the counter at the front of the list</cline>
        <cline>int i = 0;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>// Use a while loop to visit each element of the list in order</cline>
          <cline>while (i &lt; listOfNums.size())</cline>
          <cline>{</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>// Use a while loop to visit each element of the list in order</cline>
          <cline>while (i &lt;= listOfNums.size())</cline>
          <cline>{</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>    // Check for a zero and remove it</cline>
          <cline>    if (listOfNums.get(i) == 0)</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
          <cline>        listOfNums.remove(i);</cline>
          <cline>    } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>    // Check for a zero and remove it</cline>
          <cline>    if (listOfNums.get(i) == 0)</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
          <cline>        listOfNums.remove(0);</cline>
          <cline>    } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>    // Otherwise, move the counter past an element that is not zero</cline>
          <cline>    else</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
          <cline>        i++;</cline>
          <cline>    } // end else</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>    // Otherwise, move the counter past an element that is not zero</cline>
          <cline>    i++;</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>} // end while loop</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="ch8ex4muc-sgl" xml:id="ch8ex4muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following program segment is a method that should return the
        smallest int given an ArrayList of Integers (the parameter). But, the
        blocks have been mixed up and include extra blocks that are not needed
        in a correct solution. Drag the blocks from the left and put them in the
        correct order on the right. Click the Check button to check your
        solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="5">
        <cline>public static int findSmallest(ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt; nums)</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>    // Start with the first element as the smallest so far</cline>
        <cline>    int min = nums.get(0);</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>    // Use a for loop to visit each index of the list in order</cline>
          <cline>    for (int i = 0; i &lt; nums.size(); i++)</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>    // Use a for loop to visit each index of the list in order</cline>
          <cline>    for (int i = 0; i &lt;= nums.size(); i++)</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Replace the smallest so far when you find a smaller element</cline>
          <cline>        if (nums.get(i) &lt; min)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
          <cline>            min = nums.get(i);</cline>
          <cline>        } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Replace the smallest so far when you find a smaller element</cline>
          <cline>        if (nums.get(i) &gt; min)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
          <cline>            min = nums.get(i);</cline>
          <cline>        } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>    } // end for loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>    // Return the smallest integer after checking every element</cline>
        <cline>    return min;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <cline>} // end findSmallest method</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="ch8ex5muc-sgl" xml:id="ch8ex5muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following program segment is a method that should remove all the
        positive and negative odd values in an ArrayList of Integers (the
        parameter). But, the blocks have been mixed up and include extra
        blocks that are not needed in a correct solution. Drag the blocks from
        the left and put them in the correct order on the right. Click the Check
        button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="4">
        <cline>public static void removeOdd(ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt; nums)</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <cline>    // Start the counter at the front of the list</cline>
        <cline>    int i = 0;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>    // Use a while loop to visit each element of the list in order</cline>
        <cline>    while (i &lt; nums.size())</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Check for a positive or negative odd value and remove it</cline>
          <cline>        if (Math.abs(nums.get(i)) % 2 == 1)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
          <cline>            nums.remove(i);</cline>
          <cline>        } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Check for a positive or negative odd value and remove it</cline>
          <cline>        if (nums.get(i) % 2 == 1)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
          <cline>            nums.remove(i);</cline>
          <cline>        } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Otherwise, move the counter past an even value</cline>
          <cline>        else</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
          <cline>            i++;</cline>
          <cline>        } // end else</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Otherwise, move the counter past an even value</cline>
          <cline>        i++;</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>    } // end while loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <cline>} // end removeOdd method</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="ch8ex6muc-sgl" xml:id="ch8ex6muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following method should calculate the average from an ArrayList of
        Integers (the parameter). But, the blocks have been mixed up and include
        extra blocks that are not needed in a correct solution. Drag the
        needed code from the left to the right and put them in order with the
        correct indention so that the code would work correctly. Click the Check
        button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="1">
        <cline>public static double average(ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt; nums)</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>    // Start the running total at zero</cline>
          <cline>    double sum = 0;</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>    // Start the running total at zero</cline>
          <cline>    int sum = 0;</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>    // Use a for loop to visit each index of the list in order</cline>
          <cline>    for (int i = 0; i &lt; nums.size(); i++)</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>    // Use a for loop to visit each index of the list in order</cline>
          <cline>    for (int i = 0; i &lt; nums.length; i++)</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <cline>        // Add the element at this index to the running total</cline>
        <cline>        sum += nums.get(i);</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <cline>    } // end for loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>    // Turn the running total into the average and return it</cline>
        <cline>    return (sum / nums.size());</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>} // end average method</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="ch8ex7muc-sgl" xml:id="ch8ex7muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following program segment is a method that should find the largest
        value given an ArrayList of Integers (the parameter) and move it to the
        back of the list. But, the blocks have been mixed up and include extra
        blocks that are not needed in a correct solution. Drag the blocks
        from the left and put them in the correct order on the right. Click the
        Check button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="8">
        <cline>public static void moveLargest(ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt; nums)</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>    // Start with the first element's position as the largest so far</cline>
        <cline>    int largest = 0;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <cline>    // Use a for loop to visit each index of the list in order</cline>
        <cline>    for (int i = 0; i &lt; nums.size(); i++)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Replace the largest so far when you find a larger element</cline>
          <cline>        if (nums.get(i) &gt; nums.get(largest))</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
          <cline>            largest = i;</cline>
          <cline>        } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Replace the largest so far when you find a larger element</cline>
          <cline>        if (nums.get(i) &gt; nums.get(largest))</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
          <cline>            largest = nums.get(i);</cline>
          <cline>        } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Replace the largest so far when you find a larger element</cline>
          <cline>        if (nums[i] &gt; nums[largest])</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
          <cline>            largest = i;</cline>
          <cline>        } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <cline>    } // end for loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>    // Remove the largest element from the list and keep it</cline>
        <cline>    Integer largestVal = nums.remove(largest);</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="9">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>    // Put the largest element at the back of the list</cline>
          <cline>    nums.add(largestVal);</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>    // Put the largest element at the back of the list</cline>
          <cline>    nums.add(largest);</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <cline>} // end moveLargest method</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="ch8ex8muc-sgl" xml:id="ch8ex8muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following method should remove all the Strings that have length 3 or
        shorter from an ArrayList of Strings (the parameter) – so {“catch”,
        “dog”, “tree”, “me”} should become {“catch”, “tree”}. But, the blocks
        have been mixed up and include extra blocks that are not needed in a
        correct solution. Drag the needed code from the left to the right and
        put them in order with the correct indention so that the code would work
        correctly. Click the Check button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="5">
        <cline>public static void removeShort(ArrayList&lt;String&gt; words)</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>    // Start the counter at the front of the list</cline>
        <cline>    int i = 0;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>    // Use a while loop to visit each element of the list in order</cline>
        <cline>    while (i &lt; words.size())</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Check for an element of length 3 or shorter and remove it</cline>
          <cline>        if (words.get(i).length() &lt;= 3)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
          <cline>            words.remove(i);</cline>
          <cline>        } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Check for an element of length 3 or shorter and remove it</cline>
          <cline>        if (words.get(i).length &lt;= 3)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
          <cline>            words.remove(i);</cline>
          <cline>        } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Check for an element of length 3 or shorter and remove it</cline>
          <cline>        if (words.get(i).length() &lt; 3)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
          <cline>            words.remove(i);</cline>
          <cline>        } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Otherwise, move the counter past a longer element</cline>
          <cline>        else</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
          <cline>            i++;</cline>
          <cline>        } // end else</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Otherwise, move the counter past a longer element</cline>
          <cline>        i++;</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>    } // end while loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <cline>} // end removeShort method</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="ch8ex9muc-sgl" xml:id="ch8ex9muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following program segment is a method that should take each String
        from an ArrayList of Strings (the parameter) and add it again to the
        list – so {“cat”, “ribbon”, “house”} should become {“cat”, “cat”,
        “ribbon”, “ribbon”, “house”, “house”}. But, the blocks have been mixed
        up and include extra blocks that are not needed in a correct
        solution. Drag the blocks from the left and put them in the correct
        order on the right. Click the Check button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="3">
        <cline>public static void doubleList(ArrayList&lt;String&gt; words)</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>    // Start the counter at the front of the list</cline>
        <cline>    int count = 0;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>    // Use a while loop to visit each element of the list in order</cline>
          <cline>    while (count &lt; words.size())</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>    // Use a while loop to visit each element of the list in order</cline>
          <cline>    while (count &lt;= words.size())</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <cline>        // Put a copy of the element at this index right before it</cline>
        <cline>        String toAdd = words.get(count);</cline>
        <cline>        words.add(count, toAdd);</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Move the counter past both copies of the element</cline>
          <cline>        count += 2;</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Move the counter past both copies of the element</cline>
          <cline>        count++;</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <cline>    } // end while loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <cline>} // end doubleList method</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="ch8ex10muc-sgl" xml:id="ch8ex10muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The following method should remove a specific Integer (specified in
        parameter) whenever it occurs in a given ArrayList of Integers (the
        parameter). But, the blocks have been mixed up and include extra
        blocks that are not needed in a correct solution. Drag the needed code
        from the left to the right and put them in order with the correct
        indention so that the code would work correctly. Click the Check button
        to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="4">
        <cline>public static void removeElement(ArrayList&lt;Integer&gt; nums, int toRemove)</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>    // Start the counter at the front of the list</cline>
        <cline>    int i = 0;</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>    // Use a while loop to visit each element of the list in order</cline>
          <cline>    while (i &lt; nums.size())</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>    // Use a while loop to visit each element of the list in order</cline>
          <cline>    while (i &lt; nums.length)</cline>
          <cline>    {</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Check for the given integer and remove it</cline>
          <cline>        if (nums.get(i) == toRemove)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
          <cline>            nums.remove(i);</cline>
          <cline>        } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Check for the given integer and remove it</cline>
          <cline>        if (nums.get(i) == toRemove)</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
          <cline>            nums.remove(toRemove);</cline>
          <cline>        } // end if</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Otherwise, move the counter past an element that does not match</cline>
          <cline>        else</cline>
          <cline>        {</cline>
          <cline>            i++;</cline>
          <cline>        } // end else</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Otherwise, move the counter past an element that does not match</cline>
          <cline>        i++;</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>    } // end while loop</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <cline>} // end removeElement method</cline>
